# Raw downloads. Stages 1 and 2 reproduce this directory exactly, and the ten
# filings alone come to about 95 MB of inline XBRL. What the project reads out
# of those filings is preserved under references/sec_filings/.
data/raw/

# Market data, and anything that carries it. The Treasury and ECB curves could
# be redistributed, but Yahoo Finance's terms do not allow it, and the aligned
# panel mixes all three. Both files are rebuilt by scripts/02_build_factors.py.
data/interim/
data/processed/factor_moves.csv

# Everything else in data/processed is model output or figures parsed from
# public SEC filings, and is committed so results can be read without a run.

# LaTeX intermediates. main.pdf is committed, so the manuscript can be read
# without a local TeX installation, and the Overleaf archive is rebuilt by
# paper/build/package_overleaf.py rather than stored.
paper/main.aux
paper/main.bbl
paper/main.blg
paper/main.fdb_latexmk
paper/main.fls
paper/main.log
paper/main.out
paper/main.toc
paper/main.synctex.gz
paper/overleaf-gs-var.zip

# Working notes kept beside the manuscript but deliberately unpublished: the
# drafting plan, the review record and the audits of the finished draft. These
# document how the paper was made rather than what it found, and the reasoning
# for each is in paper/audit/PUBLICATION.md, which does ship.
paper/audit/outline.md
paper/audit/peer_review.md
paper/audit/prehumanization_audit.md
paper/audit/humanization_pass.md
paper/audit/open_finding_period_end.md

